## Test Directory Structure Analysis

### 1. Current Layout Overview

```
tests/
├── unit/                        # Pure unit tests (TypeScript, node:test)
├── infra/                       # Test harness, runner configs
├── providers/                   # Per-provider integration tests
│   ├── gemini/ (incl. sdk/)
│   ├── claude/
│   ├── minimax/
│   ├── deepseek/
│   ├── glm/
│   └── llama/
├── features/                    # Cross-provider feature tests
│   ├── streaming/
│   ├── thinking/
│   ├── routing/
│   └── token-counting/
├── multi-model/                 # Multi-model orchestration tests
├── api/                         # API endpoint integration tests
├── logs/                        # Test result artifacts (not code)
└── scripts/                     # Utility scripts
```

---

### 2. Purpose-Based Groupings

| Group | Files | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **`unit/`** | 6 `.test.ts` files | Pure offline unit tests using `node:test` runner — test routing helpers, token counting, auth logic, think-tag extraction, role defaults, Gemini URL construction |
| **`providers/*/`** | 16 shell scripts | Smoke/integration tests against each upstream provider (basic, models, modes, endpoints) |
| **`providers/*/sdk/`** | 6 `.js` files + 1 `.ts` file | SDK-mode tests for Gemini provider |
| **`features/*/`** | 10 files (`.sh`, `.js`, `.ts`, `.json`) | Cross-provider feature: streaming, thinking extraction, routing, token counting |
| **`api/`** | 4 `.sh` + 1 `.js` | Endpoint-level tests: `/v1/interactions`, `/v1/messages`, `/v1/responses`, `/v1/cached-content` |
| **`multi-model/`** | 6 `.sh` files | Orchestration tests with 2-5 models + oversea routing |
| **`infra/`** | 5 files (`.ts`, `.sh`, `.js`) | Test harness scripts for starting server, CI configuration, tool-blocklist erasure test |
| **`scripts/`** | 1 `.py` file | Data transform utility (dashboard dump migration) |
| **`logs/`** | ~30 files | Test run output artifacts + fix-session notes |

---

### 3. Issues & Recommendations

#### 🔴 Flagged: Misplaced / Misnamed Files

**1. [`tests/infra/tool-blocklist.ts`](file:///Users/chris/dev/bot/model_proxy_v3/tests/infra/tool-blocklist.ts) — actual unit test in wrong location**
This file directly imports `eraseBlockedTools()` from `src/utils/tool-blocklist.js` and tests it with sample bodies. It's a pure unit test but lives under `infra/` and doesn't follow the `.test.ts` naming convention, so test runners won't auto-discover it.
> **Suggestion**: Rename to `tests/unit/tool-blocklist.test.ts` and `describe`/`it` it properly.

**2. [`tests/api/sdk/integration.js`](file:///Users/chris/dev/bot/model_proxy_v3/tests/api/sdk/integration.js) — exploratory script masquerading as a test**
This ~900-line file contains inline redefinitions of helper functions (`parseDynamicRoute`, `buildTargetUrl`), duplicated test assertions in comments, and hardcoded localhost port assumptions. It also has a segment that makes live HTTP requests against a running server.
> **Suggestion**: Split into (a) a proper unit test in `tests/unit/routing.test.ts` (already exists, so add cases there) and (b) a focused integration script with a cleaner runner.

**3. [`tests/features/token-counting/sdk.ts`](file:///Users/chris/dev/bot/model_proxy_v3/tests/features/token-counting/sdk.ts) and [`local-perf.ts`](file:///Users/chris/dev/bot/model_proxy_v3/tests/features/token-counting/local-perf.ts) — TypeScript files without `.test.ts` suffix**
These won't be auto-discovered by test runners.
> **Suggestion**: Rename to `.test.ts` or add a test runner config to pick them up.

**4. [`tests/infra/config.sh`](file:///Users/chris/dev/bot/model_proxy_v3/tests/infra/config.sh) — hardcoded absolute path**
Contains `cd /home/teric/win/e/dev/bot/claude_proxy_v3` (line 3) — a machine-specific path that will fail on other machines.
> **Suggestion**: Parameterize via an environment variable, or use `$PROJECT_ROOT`.

**5. [`tests/api/v1-messages.sh`](file:///Users/chris/dev/bot/model_proxy_v3/tests/api/v1-messages.sh) — embedded API keys & massive single-file**
Contains hardcoded keys (`sk-d8d563...`) and Chinese-language test descriptions. At ~500 lines, it's a monolithic curl-driven suite better split per feature.
> **Suggestion**: Split into per-TC shell files or migrate to a structured test framework.

---

#### 🟡 Language Inconsistencies (Minor)

| Directory | Mix of Languages |
|---|---|
| `features/routing/` | `wildcard.sh` + `model.sh` ↔ `fixed.js` |
| `features/thinking/` | `basic.sh` + `cli.sh` + `models.sh` ↔ `boolean.js` |
| `providers/gemini/sdk/` | All `.js` while rest of providers use `.sh` |

> **Suggestion**: Pick a convention — either all shell scripts with a consistent assertion pattern, or migrate to a unified runner. If shell is preferred, use a shared assertion library (similar to [`tests/infra/shell.sh`](file:///Users/chris/dev/bot/model_proxy_v3/tests/infra/shell.sh)).

---

#### 🟡 Structural Suggestions

**6. Move `logs/` out of the test tree**
`tests/logs/results/` and `tests/logs/fix-sessions/` contain output artifacts from past test runs. These consume ~20+ files and don't need to live alongside test source code.
> **Suggestion**: Move to `tests_output/` at project root, or add to `.gitignore` if they're generated.

**7. Add a `tests/README.md`**
There's no documentation explaining:
- How to run unit tests (`npx tsx --test tests/unit/*.test.ts`)
- How to run integration tests (start server, then run shell scripts)
- How to add a new provider test
> **Suggestion**: Add a README with a quick-reference table.

**8. Shared assertion helpers**
Each provider `.sh` file duplicates assertion logic. [`tests/infra/shell.sh`](file:///Users/chris/dev/bot/model_proxy_v3/tests/infra/shell.sh) exists but doesn't seem to be sourced by the provider tests.
> **Suggestion**: Extract a `tests/infra/test-helpers.sh` with `assert_eq`, `assert_match`, `pass`/`fail`, and `report_summary` functions, then source it from all shell-based tests.

---

### 4. Proposed Restructuring

```diff
 tests/
-├── api/
-│   └── sdk/
